<[Gary] GARY-S> you're using the Super 8 or what else at vesta
<[jax rampant] VESTA> I had a weird bug the other dya
<[jax rampant] VESTA> no SUPER8 at vesta, but using it at home consulting.
<[Gary] GARY-S> vw's are like that
<[jax rampant] VESTA> I have a vw, but this was the weirdest programming bug I 
ever ran across.
<[Gary] GARY-S> well........
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Anyway, there was this word. COuldn't make it work. Hung 
the system every time.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Tried its components interpretively, in order, one at a 
time. Fine.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Run the word ... BYE BYE .
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Damn!
<[jax rampant] VESTA> SO ...
<[jax rampant] VESTA> It turns out that there is a part of the word that does a 
long ERASE.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> 9CC0 7C0 0 FILL
<[jax rampant] VESTA> so when the FILL ..
<[jax rampant] VESTA> gets half way thru ...
<[jax rampant] VESTA> It unsets *one single bit*, the high bit, of an address 
in a Forth definition.
<[Gary] GARY-S> you filled your program area
<[jax rampant] VESTA> changing it from 9AFF to 1AFF.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> No , i didn't ...
<[jax rampant] VESTA> the address was NO WHERE NEAR the area being filled.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Maddening!
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Turned out to be a shorted address line on the board!
<[Gary] GARY-S> I'm laughing - wait
<[jax rampant] VESTA> But all day long, you know? Ever try to convince a 
hardware engineer that it's the hardware, not your program? Dig?
<[jax rampant] VESTA> * ONE * * BIT * being set ...
<[jax rampant] VESTA> foo.
<[Gary] GARY-S> How'd you finally catch it ?
<[jax rampant] VESTA> We missed a deadline on that one ( sorta).
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Caught it by looking at it again and again.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Was the board one-ofa-kind
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Watching the D7 bit flip before&after ... yes, board was 
a pirate of one of our designs.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Competitor 'fessed up and turned self in.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> )(*&)#(*&$)(*@#&$)(*#@&
<[jax rampant] VESTA>
<[jax rampant] VESTA> .
<[Gary] GARY-S> What chips do you use - ANYthing - or some you like
<[jax rampant] VESTA> VESTA uses 8088/80188
<[jax rampant] VESTA> THough we will design anything youwant to pay for.
<[Gary] GARY-S> so you can downline from PC's ?
<[jax rampant] VESTA> Some of our boards are DOS 2.1 compatible for convenience.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> I write custom software for them & maintain the FORTH 
system.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Do you meta your code ?
<[jax rampant] VESTA> I compose on the PC, download code upload image burn rom 
OR metacompile, whatever is faster for the project.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Is the forth still on the board or only the app
<[jax rampant] VESTA> The boards have a resident FORTH, or the metacompiled app 
takes its place.
<[jax rampant] VESTA> THe VESTA idea ..
<[jax rampant] VESTA> is to provide you with everything you need on one board ..

